USB serial console
==================

One USB-C cable carries the boot log, from U-Boot proper to Linux userspace,
as a CDC ACM serial port. You also get an interactive console in U-Boot and a
login on ttyGS0 in Linux. The geni UART keeps working as before, and is still
the only place SPL's output goes.

Enabling
--------

In U-Boot proper's environment:

    => setenv usb_serial y; saveenv

How it works
------------

- U-Boot proper starts "usbacm" without waiting for the host. It queues
  everything proper printed so far (console record), then live output. A
  cyclic function services the controller every millisecond (CONFIG_CYCLIC;
  the UFS driver calls schedule() while it waits), so the host is answered
  even while nothing prints. It disconnects in board_quiesce_devices().
- Before disconnecting, U-Boot keeps answering the host for
  USB_SERIAL_SETTLE_MS. Vanishing mid control transfer (e.g. during the
  host's cdc_acm probe) stalls the host's hub for ~10 s in transfer
  timeouts, long enough to miss the kernel's g_serial completely.
- Linux gets "console=ttyGS0 g_serial.enable=1 ..." ahead of the existing
  console arguments (plus console=ttyMSM0 if there were none, to keep the
  UART), and /chosen/u-boot,usb-serial. The built-in g_serial enumerates
  during early boot. The ttyGS console buffers 256 KiB until the host opens
  the port.
- Userspace: usb-serial-gadget.service (holo usb-gadget-tools) releases
  g_serial before the configfs gadget binds and adds acm.GS0 as its first
  function. With CONFIG_U_SERIAL_CONSOLE_PERSIST the ttyGS0 console moves
  over without losing or repeating output, and adb/NCM keep working. When
  the gadget is stopped (e.g. at shutdown) the console goes back to g_serial.

Each stage re-enumerates. U-Boot and g_serial use manufacturer "Valve",
product "Steam Frame", the SoC serial number, and ACM on interface 0; the
configfs gadget keeps the serial number. That gives a stable host path, which
a reconnecting terminal follows across the gaps:

    tio /dev/serial/by-id/usb-Valve_Steam_Frame_<serial>-if00

Limitations
-----------

- If proper boots from a USB disk (BOOT_FORCE_USB, the USB boot intent or
  the boot menu's USB scan), the USB serial console is skipped or stopped,
  because those need the controller in host mode. Fastboot also takes the
  controller over.
- The console record is set up afresh after relocation, so what proper
  printed before relocation (e.g. its banner) is not in the replay.
- misc_init_r() forces bootdelay=0, so to stop at the U-Boot prompt over USB,
  also set usbconsole_enable=1 (20 s bootdelay).
